    "collapsible_content_8Pq4CU": {
      "type": "collapsible-content",
      "blocks": {
        "collapsible_row_fTHJXq": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "What if I’m claustrophobic?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>Claustrophobia is one of the most common initial concerns and people who struggle with it consistently report no problems with floating, as the lack of light in our spacious tanks (the largest available) gives more of an expansive feeling without any boundaries. <em>You also have the option to float with the lights on, lid open, or however you prefer — you’re in control of your float.</em></p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_gr4U83": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "When Can I drown if I fall asleep?I arrive for my appointment?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>No. It’s common to fall asleep for parts or sometimes all of your float and the water is so buoyant that you always stay afloat. <em>The worst that can happen is being woken by a little salt water in your eyes, though our non-drip tanks make this unlikely.</em></p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_Cb3BLt": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "How is the water cleaned?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>Our tanks are among the most hygienic systems available. The highly sterile salt water is 100% filtered between floats, as our tanks empty and refill for each float. A small amount of steriliser is added and the water is also sanitised with UV light.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_dBthLy": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "How often do you replace the water?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>Our tanks are among the most hygienic systems available. The highly sterile salt water has 525KG of medical grade Epsom salts and is 100% filtered between floats through a 1 micron filter & ozone filter, as our tanks empty and refill for each float. A small amount of steriliser is added and the water is also sanitised with UV light. The water is not wasted, but returns clean enough to drink each time (except it’s very salty)!</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_qnzyfe": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Do I need to bring anything?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>No. We have some tips and recommendations above to consider the day of your appointment, however we provide everything you need for your session.</p><p>After covid we do not provide slippers anymore, so you can bring your own slippers if you do not wish to walk barefoot or with socks that can get wet.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "collapsible_row_fTHJXq",
